# Rules & context — `LUAT_VA_BOI_CANH.md`

1. **Rule #1, no exceptions:** at the start of every session and every new task, read **`LUAT_VA_BOI_CANH.md`** at the repo root end-to-end before answering, planning, or editing. It overrides every other doc, including `huongdan.txt`.
2. Obey its working rules (section 5): reply in Vietnamese; **no code changes until the owner has agreed and the decision is recorded in section 6**.
3. Every change (new code, bug fix, config, decision) gets an entry in **section 10 (Nhật ký làm việc)** using its template, in the same session. Bug fixes must record the root cause and the lesson; reusable lessons also go into **section 9**.
4. Keep context current: before a task check sections 4, 6, 9; while working add new facts to section 8 / 9; before finishing make sure the file still matches reality. Never delete history (mark superseded). Never write real tokens or passwords.
5. `huongdan.txt` is only the technical handoff (architecture, deploy); update it when architecture or deployment changes.
